{"version":"1","id":"mwaseemzakir","handle":"mwaseemzakir","name":"Waseem .NET Newsletter","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/t_logo,f_auto/v1/logos/a10ec420048a48bf86f6889f2de88180","description":null,"is_squad":false,"x":-9.8106,"y":0.8014,"cluster_id":1,"posts_collected":68,"newest_post_at":"2025-04-26T04:25:34.500Z","oldest_post_at":"2023-03-04T06:17:34.000Z","features":{"hype_score":0.0,"listicle_ratio":0.0,"question_ratio":0.058824,"avg_read_time":2.397059,"summary_length_avg":260.529412,"title_length_avg":49.25,"title_length_var":192.863971,"tag_entropy":2.569006,"tag_diversity":0.5,"top_tag_share":0.426471,"avg_upvotes":16.661765,"median_upvotes":4.5,"avg_comments":0.529412,"comment_to_upvote_ratio":0.032628,"zero_engagement_share":0.0,"viral_share":0.044118,"posts_per_week":0.74301,"non_article_ratio":0.0,"author_present_share":0.0,"recency_skew":0.014925},"view_coords":{"engagement_style":[8.2794,0.5294],"cadence_depth":[-2.3529,-7.1765],"hype_variety":[-6.3235,-5.8971],"title_style":[6.5441,-4.2206]},"top_tags":[[".net",55],[".net-core",23],["c#",17],["webdev",12],["dependency-injection",6],["design-patterns",5],["database",5],["nuget",4]],"sample_titles":{"representative":["A Comprehensive Guide to the Top 18 .NET Libraries Every Developer Should Know","EP 58 : Fluent Validation in .NET","EP 66 : Clean Code Tips for .NET Developers - Part I"],"outlier":["EP 15 : What is CORS (Cross Origin Resource Sharing ) and how to enable them in .NET Core 6.0?"]},"recent_posts":[{"id":"Hf40PYIm2","title":"Wolverine as Mediator in .NET","url":"https://mwaseemzakir.substack.com/p/wolverine-as-mediator-in-net","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/wolverine-as-mediator-in-net-hf40pyim2","summary":"With MediatR going commercial, developers are exploring alternatives. Wolverine, a free NuGet package, offers next-generation .NET mediator and message bus capabilities. Using Wolverine involves simple naming conventions and no special interfaces, making it a streamlined choice for handling messages in .NET applications. It includes features like fluent validation and can be configured to use only core mediator services to keep applications lean and efficient.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/096e73aaeafe35a51b2882eae10ac4e0?_a=AQAEuj9","num_upvotes":11,"num_comments":2,"created_at":"2025-04-26T04:25:34.500Z"},{"id":"gC4SpBcyq","title":"Setting Up OpenAI Chat in a .NET API","url":"https://mwaseemzakir.substack.com/p/setting-up-openai-chat-in-a-net-api","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/setting-up-openai-chat-in-a-net-api-gc4spbcyq","summary":"Learn how to integrate OpenAI's Chat API into your .NET application in three simple steps: obtaining your API key, installing the required NuGet package, and configuring your code. The post covers basic setup, methods and properties of the `ChatClient`, and best practices for robust implementation including handling models, securing API keys, and error management.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/8732f7353218543d24da35d3bf7e16e1?_a=AQAEuj9","num_upvotes":14,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-11-02T06:16:47.615Z"},{"id":"eiCPKG4Yk","title":"Data Annotations in C#","url":"https://mwaseemzakir.substack.com/p/data-annotations-in-c","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/data-annotations-in-c--eicpkg4yk","summary":"Learn how to implement data annotations for data validation in C#. The post covers common validation attributes such as [Required], [StringLength], [Range], [RegularExpression], and more with code examples. Data annotations offer a simple way to ensure only valid data reaches your database and can also serve purposes like specifying display formats, primary keys, and foreign key relationships.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/b27b8d33ce3340c5803e88161e089399?_a=AQAEuiZ","num_upvotes":9,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-10-26T06:07:40.716Z"},{"id":"39mpT4D5u","title":"A Comprehensive Guide to the Top 18 .NET Libraries Every Developer Should Know","url":"https://mwaseemzakir.substack.com/p/top-15-essential-net-libraries-for","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/top-18-essential-net-libraries-for-developers-39mpt4d5u","summary":"A guide to 18 essential .NET libraries for developers, detailing their use cases, benefits, and trivia. Libraries include Mediator for CQRS, Dapper for micro-ORM, Serilog for logging, and more. Each library is briefly explained with implementation links provided.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/03aa4d72e8c209c11456cda27cad4cc7?_a=AQAEuiZ","num_upvotes":186,"num_comments":6,"created_at":"2024-10-05T06:01:36.000Z"},{"id":"VxkZa6o3T","title":"EP 66 : Clean Code Tips for .NET Developers - Part I","url":"https://mwaseemzakir.substack.com/p/ep-66-clean-code-tips-for-net-developers","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/ep-66-clean-code-tips-for-net-developers---part-i-vxkza6o3t","summary":"This post provides clean code tips for .NET developers, focusing on giving meaningful names, avoiding null returns, keeping class and method sizes small, not reinventing the wheel, and using appropriate tools or IDEs. It also offers practical examples and suggestions for better coding practices in .NET projects.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/2bfaacd665127c182808b1d96e51d8fb?_a=AQAEuiZ","num_upvotes":102,"num_comments":10,"created_at":"2024-09-28T06:03:24.000Z"},{"id":"RzJSkERo4","title":"EP 65 : Primary Constructor in C#","url":"https://mwaseemzakir.substack.com/p/ep-65-primary-constructor-in-c","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/ep-65-primary-constructor-in-c--rzjskero4","summary":"Primary constructors in .NET 8 and C# 12 offer a cleaner way of constructor initialization by reducing boilerplate code, simplifying syntax, and enhancing readability. An example compares the traditional constructor injection with primary constructors, highlighting their advantages.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/b29cc2b407e216665c4c5b02c3c1bba0?_a=AQAEuiZ","num_upvotes":27,"num_comments":1,"created_at":"2024-07-06T09:20:42.000Z"},{"id":"ZY1jbRWnL","title":"EP 64 : Service Locator Pattern in .NET","url":"https://mwaseemzakir.substack.com/p/ep-64-service-locator-pattern-in","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/ep-64-service-locator-pattern-in-net-zy1jbrwnl","summary":"The service locator pattern in .NET allows for the injection and retrieval of services via a central service provider. It's useful in scenarios where dependency injection isn't feasible, such as dealing with service scope mismatches or updating legacy code. Although practical, it has drawbacks, including testing complications and potential for poor design choices. Direct dependency injection is generally preferred for its cleaner and more manageable structure.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/7b14a7a772eb91e40ea8c8d6b5c17686?_a=AQAEuiZ","num_upvotes":22,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-06-22T06:56:47.000Z"},{"id":"AGvXK5sJN","title":"EP 63 : Keyed Service Dependency Injection in .NET","url":"https://mwaseemzakir.substack.com/p/ep-63-keyed-service-dependency-injection","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/ep-63-keyed-service-dependency-injection-in-net-agvxk5sjn","summary":"This post discusses Dependency Injection in .NET, including the difference between Singleton, Scoped, and Transient, the concept of Keyed Services in .NET 8, and how to achieve the same behavior in older versions of .NET.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/734b07865ee55ff913f3a3109f1f183b?_a=AQAEuiZ","num_upvotes":12,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-06-15T07:29:17.000Z"},{"id":"GBIpFYd8V","title":"EP 62 : Dependency Injection Explained in .NET","url":"https://mwaseemzakir.substack.com/p/ep-62-dependency-injection-explained","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/ep-62-dependency-injection-explained-in-net-gbipfyd8v","summary":"Dependency injection is a programming technique in which an object receives other required objects instead of creating them internally. Benefits of dependency injection include automatic handling of object creation and disposal, easy unit testing, and adaptability to changes without affecting existing code. Dependency injection can be implemented using the singleton, transient, or scoped approach.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/f6a99d878defdf3937c661b6c5af1e3a?_a=AQAEuiZ","num_upvotes":97,"num_comments":1,"created_at":"2024-06-08T06:56:40.000Z"},{"id":"HoVpSw2L2","title":"EP 61 : Custom Type Handling with Dapper in .NET","url":"https://mwaseemzakir.substack.com/p/ep-61-custom-type-handling-with-dapper-7ce","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/ep-61-custom-type-handling-with-dapper-in-net-hovpsw2l2","summary":"Learn how to handle complex types with Dapper using custom type handlers in .NET.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/52f783421697c51d29483dce1f1f1620?_a=AQAEuiZ","num_upvotes":23,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-06-03T01:42:12.000Z"}],"similar_handles":["codeheim","angularlove","phoenix-files","bun","webdevbeehiiv"],"opposite_handles":["felixrieseberg","tbpn","alexfinn","ryolu_","hamelhusain"],"similar":[{"id":"codeheim","handle":"codeheim","name":"codeHeim","is_squad":false,"x":-9.9395,"y":0.9232,"cluster_id":1,"posts_collected":86,"image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--DSlJJUu6--/f_auto/v1710002834/logos/codeheim","features_preview":{"posts_per_week":1.470102,"median_upvotes":13.0,"author_present_share":0.0,"hype_score":0.005814,"avg_read_time":9.465116,"tag_diversity":0.534884},"top_tags_preview":[["golang",83],["webdev",25],["backend",8]],"view_coords":{"engagement_style":[8.3235,-5.25],"cadence_depth":[-1.2